## 📝 1. Nano Text Editor

`nano` is a simple terminal-based text editor that can be used to create and modify files.

### Open or create a file

```bash
nano myfile
```

### Important Nano shortcuts

| Shortcut   | Function             |
| ---------- | -------------------- |
| `Ctrl + X` | Exit Nano            |
| `Ctrl + O` | Save/write the file  |
| `Ctrl + W` | Search               |
| `Ctrl + K` | Cut a line           |
| `Ctrl + U` | Paste                |
| `Ctrl + G` | Help                 |
| `Ctrl + _` | Go to line           |
| `Ctrl + C` | Show cursor position |

### Example

```bash
nano notes.txt
```

I can then enter multiple lines of text and save the file using:

```text
Ctrl + O
Enter
Ctrl + X
```

