## 🌐 3. Downloading Files with Wget

`wget` can download files from a web server using HTTP or HTTPS.

### Basic syntax

```bash
wget <URL>
```

### Example

```bash
wget https://example.com/file.txt
```

The downloaded file will normally be saved in the current directory.

Useful for downloading:

* Scripts
* Text files
* Programs
* Other resources

