## 🌍 5. Python HTTP Server

Python includes a lightweight HTTP server that can be used to quickly serve files from a directory.

### Start the server

```bash
python3 -m http.server
```

By default, it runs on:

```text
Port: 8000
```

You can then access the files from another machine using:

```bash
wget http://<IP>:8000/<filename>
```

### Example

On the machine containing the files:

```bash
python3 -m http.server
```

From another machine:

```bash
wget http://10.49.138.37:8000/file
```

### Important

The terminal running the Python server must remain active.

You can open another terminal to download the file.

